\noindent \begin{minipage}{\linewidth } \scriptsize\includegraphics[width=0.7\linewidth ]{Figures/Figure_MelatoninBehaviourPhenotype_stats.png}\par \textbf {Figure~1---figure supplement 1.} Quantification of epoch-level behavioural responses from \emph {\textbf {\oldautoref {fig:1}}} \\ Distributions of responsiveness for different epochs of the experiment \textbf {ii)-vi)}: \textbf {ii)} Naive Response (first 3 dark-flash stimuli), \textbf {iii)} Block 1 (remaining 57 stimuli of the first training block), \textbf {iv)} Trained Response (training blocks 2--4), \textbf {v)} Acoustic Response (30 vibration stimuli), and \textbf {vi)} Re-test Block (Block 5, 5 hours after the final training block). Each dot is the per-fish average of the epoch. Statistical significance was calculated using the Kruskal-Wallis test followed by Dunn's test for post-hoc pairwise comparisons, * = p < 0.05, ** = p < 0.01, *** = p < 0.001. \\ \textbf {A)} The probability of response to the stimulus, \\ \textbf {B)} the response latency, \\ \textbf {C)} the maximum tail-bend amplitude achieved during the movement, \\ \textbf {D)} the duration of the movement, \\ \textbf {E)} the displacement of the movement, and \\ \textbf {F)} the reorientation achieved by the larvae. \par \vskip 8pt \end{minipage} \vskip 16pt 
